    "faq_FKqUjK": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_row_6L8JYN": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q1. What do your AI SEO Singapore packages cover?",
            "answer": "<p>Our AI SEO packages help businesses in Singapore improve how their brands are understood and represented in AI-generated answers. The work combines customer-question research, website and content improvements, brand information consistency, external-source recommendations and monitoring. This AI-search work is also known as GEO. A full traditional SEO program is scoped separately; target markets and languages are agreed before work begins.<br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_Nxk7Qg": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q2.  Which plan and AI channels should we choose?",
            "answer": "<p>Essential covers one selected channel: ChatGPT or Google AI Overviews. Growth covers ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, Gemini and Perplexity. We help you choose based on your audience, target markets and customer research behaviour. Google AI Overviews and Gemini are monitored separately. Google AI Mode is not included unless agreed.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_XiLH9X": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q3.  What do the question, page and FAQ quantities mean?",
            "answer": "<p>The 50 or 100 core questions form the total agreed question library. A page optimization is an agreed improvement to an existing page. An FAQ set is a group of related questions and answers for one page or topic. Questions per FAQ set and the depth of page work are confirmed before delivery.<br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_X4L7Gj": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q4.  How do you measure progress, and can you guarantee results?",
            "answer": "<p>We monitor brand mentions, recommendation context, citations, accuracy and competitor presence across an agreed question sample. Identifiable AI referral visits and relevant website actions are reviewed where tracking allows. Results reflect the monitored sample; specific recommendations, citations, rankings or leads cannot be guaranteed.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_tGbwJD": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q5.   What do we provide, and who publishes or implements the work?",
            "answer": "<p>Provide your goals, priority products or services, markets, competitors and approved brand information. Website, analytics or publishing access may be needed. Content approval, publishing and technical implementation responsibilities are agreed during onboarding. Paid placements, third-party fees and substantial development are scoped separately.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_RhamPq": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Q6.  Why is the minimum engagement six months?",
            "answer": "<p>The program needs time to establish a baseline, deliver improvements and review repeated observations. The first 90 days focus on building the foundation, progressing content and reviewing early findings. Your proposal confirms the delivery schedule. Renewal or scope changes are agreed in writing.<br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
